    title: "Public repositories",
    body: "Your documented rules checked on every public pull request, with a diagram of each change, plus the browser extension for any public PR you visit.",
    price: "$0",
    priceDetail: "forever"
  },
  {
    eyebrow: "Starter",
    icon: "team",
    title: "One team's private repos",
    body: "Your documented rules checked on every private pull request, with a diagram of each change, for one team\u2019s repositories.",
    price: "$29",
    priceDetail: "/mo · 5 repos"
  },
  {
    eyebrow: "Enterprise",
    icon: "gear",
    title: "Self-hosted & 50+ repos",
    body: "Private deployment, SSO, and audit workflows for organizations that need full control.",
    price: "",
    priceDetail: "Talk to us"
  }
];

---

<BaseLayout
  title="Striff - Your documented architecture, checked on every pull request"
  description="Striff reads your AGENTS.md, ADRs and architecture docs, turns each sentence about the code into a checkable rule, and answers it on every GitHub pull request, with a diagram of what changed and review notes on the components it touched."
  canonical="https://striff.io/"
  ogImage="https://striff.io/og-image.png"
>
  <main>
    <!-- ==================== HERO ==================== -->
    <!-- The product is a GitHub check, so the hero is one, rendered light and at full
         fidelity: an illustrative example (acme/checkout-service, labelled Example), not a
         real run. Each row is the sentence, the file and line it is on, the rule it became,
         and what happened to it on this pull request; the broken row leads because that is
         the row a reviewer needs first. The real ecChronos run is in the report below. -->
    <section class="hero-section relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-[90rem] px-6">
        <div class="hero-copy relative z-10 mx-auto max-w-4xl space-y-5 text-center" data-reveal>
          <h1 class="mx-auto">
            <span class="sr-only">Your architecture docs, enforced on every pull request.</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true">Your <span class="h1-rot" data-h1-rot><span class="h1-rot-word is-on">architecture docs</span><span class="h1-rot-word">design docs</span><span class="h1-rot-word">AGENTS.md</span></span>,<br /> <span class="hero-h1-accent">enforced on every pull request</span>.</span>
          </h1>
          <p class="section-subcopy hero-subcopy mx-auto">
            Your docs already state the rules. Striff checks every pull request against them, and <strong>when a change contradicts one, it quotes the sentence, before the merge.</strong>
          </p>

          <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3 pt-2">
            <a class="btn-primary btn-primary-lg" href={githubAppUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              <svg class="h-4 w-4" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.01-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82.64-.18 1.32-.27 2-.27s1.36.09 2 .27c1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.01 8.01 0 0 0 16 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8z" />
              </svg>
              Install the GitHub App
            </a>
            <a class="btn-secondary btn-secondary-lg" href="#pipeline">How it works</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-check-wrap" data-reveal>
          <div class="hero-check-card">
            <!-- Styled as the check it is, and in the same clothes as the real one further down
                 the page, so a reader meets one idea twice rather than two designs once. The
                 branch and the pull request number are the part that was missing: without them
                 the card was a table of rules with no occasion. -->
            <header class="hcc-head ghcheck-head">
              <span class="ghcheck-mark"><img src="/icon.svg" alt="" width="18" height="18" /></span>
              <!-- A check exists on a pull request, and the header is the only thing that says
                   which one. It used to say it in the same small mono line as the branch, where
                   the number a reviewer would quote was the least visible thing on the card. -->
              <span class="ghcheck-title">
                <b>
                  Striff
                  <span class="ghcheck-on">on</span>
                  <span class="ghcheck-pr">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="13" height="13" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M1.5 3.25a2.25 2.25 0 1 1 3 2.122v5.256a2.251 2.251 0 1 1-1.5 0V5.372A2.25 2.25 0 0 1 1.5 3.25Zm5.677-.177L9.573.677A.25.25 0 0 1 10 .854V2.5h1A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 13.5 5v5.628a2.251 2.251 0 1 1-1.5 0V5a1 1 0 0 0-1-1h-1v1.646a.25.25 0 0 1-.427.177L7.177 3.427a.25.25 0 0 1 0-.354ZM3.75 2.5a.75.75 0 1 0 0 1.5.75.75 0 0 0 0-1.5Zm0 9.5a.75.75 0 1 0 0 1.5.75.75 0 0 0 0-1.5Zm8.25.75a.75.75 0 1 0 1.5 0 .75.75 0 0 0-1.5 0Z"/></svg>
                    Pull request #418
                  </span>
                </b>
                <i>{heroExampleRepo} &middot; feat/csv-export &rarr; main</i>
              </span>
              <span class="ghcheck-state is-bad">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="13" height="13" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.343 13.657A8 8 0 1 1 13.658 2.343 8 8 0 0 1 2.343 13.657ZM6.03 4.97a.751.751 0 0 0-1.06 1.06L6.94 8 4.97 9.97a.75.75 0 1 0 1.06 1.06L8 9.06l1.97 1.97a.75.75 0 0 0 1.06-1.06L9.06 8l1.97-1.97a.75.75 0 0 0-1.06-1.06L8 6.94Z"/></svg>
                1 rule broken
              </span>
            </header>

            <div class="hcc-banner">
              <span class="hcc-banner-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <p class="hcc-banner-text">
                <strong>One of the {heroExampleTally.broken + heroExampleTally.held} rules Striff checked in this repository&rsquo;s own docs no longer holds.</strong>
                <span>Nothing was configured.</span>
              </p>
              <span class="hcc-tally">
                <span class="hcc-tally-item hcc-tally-violated"><b>{heroExampleTally.broken}</b><i>broken</i></span>
                <span class="hcc-tally-item hcc-tally-held"><b>{heroExampleTally.held}</b><i>held</i></span>
              </span>
            </div>

            <RuleRows rows={heroExampleRules} />
          </div>
          <!-- The notation named once, where it is being looked at. Without this the formulas
               are a signal that something is being computed; with it they are the thing being
               computed, which is the claim the whole page rests on. -->
          <p class="hero-check-more">
            <Formula tex={String.raw`\varphi`} /> is the rule compiled to a formula,
            <Formula tex={String.raw`\mathcal{M}`} /> your code parsed at each revision; the
            verdict is whether one satisfies the other. Three of the {heroExampleTally.broken + heroExampleTally.held} rules
            this repository&rsquo;s docs state. <a href="/demo">The dashboard lists all of them &rarr;</a>
          </p>
          <div class="hero-langs" aria-label="Supported languages">
            <span class="hero-langs-label">Works with</span>
            {heroLanguages.map((lang) => (
              <span class="lang-chip" style={`--lang: ${lang.color}`}>
                <span class="lang-chip-mark" aria-hidden="true">{lang.mark}</span>
                {lang.name}
              </span>
            ))}
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ==================== PROBLEM ==================== -->
    <section id="problem" class="scroll-mt-24 bg-slate-100/60 pb-16 pt-14">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-[90rem] px-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="rounded-3xl bg-white p-6 shadow-xl border border-slate-200 md:p-8">
          <div class="problem-split">
            <div class="problem-copy">
              <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-rose-500">The problem</p>
              <h2 class="mt-3 text-balance">Nobody re-reads the docs on every pull request.</h2>
              <p class="section-subcopy mt-4">
                Coding agents read your architecture docs as context, then write code that quietly contradicts them, and no reviewer re-reads those documents on every change to catch it. Left unchecked, each merge drifts a little further from what your team agreed, until <strong>every change costs more than it should and nobody wants to touch the core</strong>. Striff catches the contradiction on the pull request, while it is still a one-line fix.
              </p>
              <p class="problem-stat">
                In <a href="/blog/architecture-matters-more-not-less">our survey of 335 open-source repositories</a> that write their architecture down, <strong>63% already hand their coding agents docs to build from</strong>, and <strong>only 8% of those run anything that checks the code still matches.</strong>
              </p>
              <BlogLink slug="architecture-matters-more-not-less" kicker="Why coding agents make architecture review matter more" class="mt-6" />
            </div>

            <!-- The firehose, run by agents: every lane is an agent's branch and every row in the
                 feed is an agent acting on the repo. -->
            <figure class="gs" data-reveal aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="0" height="0" style="position:absolute"><defs><linearGradient id="gs-gemini" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#4f8df9" /><stop offset="55%" stop-color="#9b72cb" /><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#d96570" /></linearGradient></defs></svg>
              <div class="gs-head">
                <span class="gs-live"><span class="gs-live-dot"></span><span class="gs-live-repo">5 agents</span> working on acme-corp</span>
                <span class="gs-head-tag">last hour</span>
              </div>
              <div class="gs-body">
                <div class="gs-col">
                  <span class="gs-col-head">agent branches → main</span>
                  <div class="gs-graph">
                  <div class="gs-graph-scroll">
                    {[0, 1].map(() => (
                      <svg class="gs-graph-unit" viewBox="0 0 140 320" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">
                        <path class="gs-line gs-line-main" d="M30 0 L30 320" />
                        <path class="gs-line gs-line-a" d="M30 256 C 52 256 70 242 70 218 L 70 172 C 70 148 52 144 30 144" />
                        <path class="gs-line gs-line-b" d="M30 224 C 60 224 104 206 104 178 L 104 92 C 104 66 60 64 30 64" />
                        <circle class="gs-dot gs-dot-main" cx="30" cy="32" r="5" />
                        <circle class="gs-dot gs-dot-main" cx="30" cy="96" r="5" />
                        <circle class="gs-dot gs-dot-main" cx="30" cy="160" r="5" />
                        <circle class="gs-dot gs-dot-main" cx="30" cy="224" r="5" />
                        <circle class="gs-dot gs-dot-main" cx="30" cy="288" r="5" />
                        <g class="gs-agent gs-agent-a"><circle cx="70" cy="196" r="9.5" class="gs-agent-bg" /><g transform="translate(64 190) scale(0.5)"><g class="gs-agent-mark"><path d="M11.04 19.32Q12 21.51 12 24q0-2.49.93-4.68.96-2.19 2.58-3.81t3.81-2.55Q21.51 12 24 12q-2.49 0-4.68-.93a12.3 12.3 0 0 1-3.81-2.58 12.3 12.3 0 0 1-2.58-3.81Q12 2.49 12 0q0 2.49-.96 4.68-.93 2.19-2.55 3.81a12.3 12.3 0 0 1-3.81 2.58Q2.49 12 0 12q2.49 0 4.68.96 2.19.93 3.81 2.55t2.55 3.81" /></g></g></g>
                        <g class="gs-agent gs-agent-b"><circle cx="104" cy="168" r="9.5" class="gs-agent-bg" /><g transform="translate(98 162) scale(0.5)"><g class="gs-agent-mark"><path d="m4.7144 15.9555 4.7174-2.6471.079-.2307-.079-.1275h-.2307l-.7893-.0486-2.6956-.0729-2.3375-.0971-2.2646-.1214-.5707-.1215-.5343-.7042.0546-.3522.4797-.3218.686.0608 1.5179.1032 2.2767.1578 1.6514.0972 2.4468.255h.3886l.0546-.1579-.1336-.0971-.1032-.0972L6.973 9.8356l-2.55-1.6879-1.3356-.9714-.7225-.4918-.3643-.4614-.1578-1.0078.6557-.7225.8803.0607.2246.0607.8925.686 1.9064 1.4754 2.4893 1.8336.3643.3035.1457-.1032.0182-.0728-.164-.2733-1.3539-2.4467-1.445-2.4893-.6435-1.032-.17-.6194c-.0607-.255-.1032-.4674-.1032-.7285L6.287.1335 6.6997 0l.9957.1336.419.3642.6192 1.4147 1.0018 2.2282 1.5543 3.0296.4553.8985.2429.8318.091.255h.1579v-.1457l.1275-1.706.2368-2.0947.2307-2.6957.0789-.7589.3764-.9107.7468-.4918.5828.2793.4797.686-.0668.4433-.2853 1.8517-.5586 2.9021-.3643 1.9429h.2125l.2429-.2429.9835-1.3053 1.6514-2.0643.7286-.8196.85-.9046.5464-.4311h1.0321l.759 1.1293-.34 1.1657-1.0625 1.3478-.8804 1.1414-1.2628 1.7-.7893 1.36.0729.1093.1882-.0183 2.8535-.607 1.5421-.2794 1.8396-.3157.8318.3886.091.3946-.3278.8075-1.967.4857-2.3072.4614-3.4364.8136-.0425.0304.0486.0607 1.5482.1457.6618.0364h1.621l3.0175.2247.7892.522.4736.6376-.079.4857-1.2142.6193-1.6393-.3886-3.825-.9107-1.3113-.3279h-.1822v.1093l1.0929 1.0686 2.0035 1.8092 2.5075 2.3314.1275.5768-.3218.4554-.34-.0486-2.2039-1.6575-.85-.7468-1.9246-1.621h-.1275v.17l.4432.6496 2.3436 3.5214.1214 1.0807-.17.3521-.6071.2125-.6679-.1214-1.3721-1.9246L14.38 17.959l-1.1414-1.9428-.1397.079-.674 7.2552-.3156.3703-.7286.2793-.6071-.4614-.3218-.7468.3218-1.4753.3886-1.9246.3157-1.53.2853-1.9004.17-.6314-.0121-.0425-.1397.0182-1.4328 1.9672-2.1796 2.9446-1.7243 1.8456-.4128.164-.7164-.3704.0667-.6618.4008-.5889 2.386-3.0357 1.4389-1.882.929-1.0868-.0062-.1579h-.0546l-6.3385 4.1164-1.1293.1457-.4857-.4554.0608-.7467.2307-.2429 1.9064-1.3114Z" /></g></g></g>
                        <circle class="gs-dot gs-dot-b" cx="104" cy="102" r="4.5" />
                        <circle class="gs-merge gs-merge-a" cx="30" cy="144" r="6.5" />
                        <circle class="gs-merge gs-merge-b" cx="30" cy="64" r="6.5" />
                      </svg>
                    ))}
                  </div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="gs-col gs-col-feed">
                  <span class="gs-col-head">activity</span>
                  <div class="gs-feed">
                  <div class="gs-feed-scroll">
                    {[0, 1].map(() => activityFeed.map((a) => (
                      <div class={`gs-item ${agentClass[a.agent]}`}>
                        <span class="gs-item-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d={agentIcon[a.agent]} /></svg></span>
                        <span class="gs-item-text"><b>{agentName[a.agent]}</b> {a.text}</span>
                        <span class="gs-item-meta">{a.time}</span>
                      </div>
                    )))}
                  </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <figcaption class="gs-caption">They all read your architecture docs. <strong>Nothing checks that they followed them.</strong></figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ==================== THE DIAGRAM ==================== -->
    <!-- The structural diff, kept exactly as it was but no longer opening the page. The
         rules are what nobody else does; this is what the same check draws beside them, and
         it earns a full stage of its own here rather than competing with the headline. -->
    <section id="diagram" class="diagram-section scroll-mt-24 pb-16 pt-16">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-[90rem] px-6">
        <div class="diagram-intro max-w-3xl" data-reveal>
          <p class="examples-kicker">The check</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-balance">What Striff posts on a pull request.</h2>
          <p class="section-subcopy mt-4">
            One check, beside your CI. It says what the change moved, lists every rule your own documents state about the code it touched, says whether each one still holds and quotes the sentence it came from, and draws the classes involved.
          </p>
          <p class="diagram-source">
            <span class="diagram-source-label">Below is one, unedited, from a public repository:</span>
            <a class="diagram-source-pr" href="https://github.com/catatafishen/agentbridge/pull/1102" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              catatafishen/agentbridge #1102
            </a>
            <a class="diagram-source-run" href="https://github.com/catatafishen/agentbridge/runs/108628049213" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the check itself &rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- The check as GitHub renders it: the summary, the rules table in the three columns the
             check actually posts, and the diagram, which the check embeds at the end of the same
             comment. Split across two sections it asked a reader to believe they were one run. -->
        <div class="check-report" data-reveal>
          <div class="ghcheck">
            <div class="ghcheck-head">
              <span class="ghcheck-mark"><img src="/icon.svg" alt="" width="18" height="18" /></span>
              <span class="ghcheck-title">
                <b>Striff</b>
                <i>catatafishen/agentbridge &middot; #1102 &middot; fix/issues-1074-and-later</i>
              </span>
              <span class="ghcheck-state">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="13" height="13" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13.78 4.22a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.06l-7.25 7.25a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06 0L2.22 9.28a.751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018L6 10.94l6.72-6.72a.75.75 0 0 1 1.06 0Z"/></svg>
                Successful
              </span>
            </div>

            <div class="ghcheck-body">
              <h3 class="ghcheck-h">Documented Rules</h3>
              <p class="ghcheck-note">Rules read from this repository&rsquo;s own docs and checked against the dependency graph this PR produces.</p>

              <div class="ghcheck-table-wrap">
                <table class="ghcheck-table">
                  <thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Source</th><th>This PR</th></tr></thead>
                  <tbody>
                    {realCheckRules.map((r) => (
                      <tr>
                        <td class="ghcheck-rule"><InlineCodeText text={r.rule} /></td>
                        <td class="ghcheck-src"><code>{r.doc}</code><span>{r.quote}</span></td>
                        <td class="ghcheck-verdict"><span class="ghcheck-holds">&#10003; holds</span></td>
                      </tr>
                    ))}
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
              <p class="ghcheck-more">{24 - realCheckRules.length} more rules checked, all held.</p>

              <!-- The diagram is not a second section. The check embeds it here, at the end of the
                   same comment, and it is wide because a real architecture is wide. -->
              <figure class="ghcheck-figure">
                <!-- The whole diagram, opened on the git tools. Cropping the SVG instead meant
                     panning ran off the edge of the file into white; a window onto the real thing
                     has more diagram in every direction, which is what a reader expects when a
                     caption invites them to drag. The whole diagram is a click away and the
                     frame pans and zooms, which is what the extension does on GitHub itself. -->
                <div
                  class="ghcheck-diagram"
                  data-panzoom
                  data-focus-x="10120"
                  data-focus-y="1708"
                  data-focus-w="1313"
                  data-focus-h="465"
                >
                  <img src="/examples/agentbridge-1102-diagram.svg" width="12796" height="3793" alt="Striff's diagram of catatafishen/agentbridge pull request 1102: the fifty classes the change touched and how they connect, opened on the git tools, with added members in green, removed in red and changed in blue" loading="lazy" draggable="false" data-panzoom-img />
                  <!-- What the colours mean, at the moment of looking at them. As prose under
                       the frame this was a sentence nobody read on the way past; as three chips
                       on the diagram it answers the question the diagram raises. -->
                  <p class="ghcheck-legend">
                    <span class="is-add">added</span>
                    <span class="is-del">removed</span>
                    <span class="is-mod">changed</span>
                    <em>one box, one class</em>
                  </p>
                  <div class="ghcheck-zoom" role="group" aria-label="Zoom the diagram">
                    <button type="button" data-panzoom-out aria-label="Zoom out">&minus;</button>
                    <button type="button" data-panzoom-reset>Reset</button>
                    <button type="button" data-panzoom-in aria-label="Zoom in">+</button>
                    <button type="button" data-panzoom-max aria-label="Maximize the diagram" title="Maximize">
                      <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                        <path d="M6 2.5H2.5V6" /><path d="M10 2.5h3.5V6" /><path d="M6 13.5H2.5V10" /><path d="M10 13.5h3.5V10" />
                      </svg>
                    </button>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </figure>

              <p class="ghcheck-caption">
                Every check carries a <b>structural diff diagram</b>. It draws the part of your
                architecture that the pull request touched, in UML class notation: a box for each
                class, its members inside it, and a line for each dependency between them. Colour
                marks what the change added, removed and altered. Drag it to pan, or open it full
                size.
              </p>

              <p class="ghcheck-foot">
                <img src="/icon.svg" alt="" width="14" height="14" />
                <span><b>Striff</b> maps how this pull request changes the architecture and checks it against the rules written in the repository&rsquo;s own docs.</span>
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <script is:inline>
        // Pan and zoom for the diagram inside the check. The extension does this on GitHub; here
        // it is the difference between a picture of a diagram and a diagram.
        (function () {
          var frame = document.querySelector("[data-panzoom]");
          if (!frame) return;
          var img = frame.querySelector("[data-panzoom-img]");
          // The image is laid out at the diagram's own size, so one unit of scale is one SVG
          // unit. Home is whatever scale and offset puts the focus region in the frame; from
          // there every direction has more diagram in it rather than more nothing.
          var FX = +frame.dataset.focusX, FY = +frame.dataset.focusY;
          var FW = +frame.dataset.focusW, FH = +frame.dataset.focusH;
          var k = 1, tx = 0, ty = 0, dragging = false, lastX = 0, lastY = 0;

          function apply() {
            img.style.transform = "translate(" + tx + "px," + ty + "px) scale(" + k + ")";
          }
          function zoom(next, ox, oy) {
            next = Math.min(2.5, Math.max(0.06, next));
            var box = frame.getBoundingClientRect();
            var cx = (ox === undefined ? box.width / 2 : ox) - tx;
            var cy = (oy === undefined ? box.height / 2 : oy) - ty;
            tx -= cx * (next / k - 1);
            ty -= cy * (next / k - 1);
            k = next;
            apply();
          }
          function fit() {
            var box = frame.getBoundingClientRect();
            if (!box.width || !box.height) return;
            k = Math.min(box.width / FW, box.height / FH);
            tx = -FX * k + (box.width - FW * k) / 2;
            ty = -FY * k + (box.height - FH * k) / 2;
            apply();
          }

          frame.addEventListener("pointerdown", function (e) {
            if (e.target.closest(".ghcheck-zoom")) return;
            dragging = true; lastX = e.clientX; lastY = e.clientY;
            frame.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);
            frame.classList.add("is-grabbing");
          });
          frame.addEventListener("pointermove", function (e) {
            if (!dragging) return;
            tx += e.clientX - lastX; ty += e.clientY - lastY;
            lastX = e.clientX; lastY = e.clientY;
            apply();
          });
          function release(e) {
            if (!dragging) return;
            dragging = false;
            frame.classList.remove("is-grabbing");
            try { frame.releasePointerCapture(e.pointerId); } catch (err) {}
          }
          frame.addEventListener("pointerup", release);
          frame.addEventListener("pointercancel", release);
          // Ctrl/meta-free wheel still scrolls the page unless the pointer is over the frame and
          // the reader means to zoom, which is what the deliberate preventDefault is for.
          frame.addEventListener("wheel", function (e) {
            e.preventDefault();
            var box = frame.getBoundingClientRect();
            zoom(k * (e.deltaY < 0 ? 1.12 : 1 / 1.12), e.clientX - box.left, e.clientY - box.top);
          }, { passive: false });

          var inBtn = frame.querySelector("[data-panzoom-in]");
          var outBtn = frame.querySelector("[data-panzoom-out]");
          var resetBtn = frame.querySelector("[data-panzoom-reset]");
          if (inBtn) inBtn.addEventListener("click", function () { zoom(k * 1.25); });
          if (outBtn) outBtn.addEventListener("click", function () { zoom(k / 1.25); });
          if (resetBtn) resetBtn.addEventListener("click", fit);
          var maxBtn = frame.querySelector("[data-panzoom-max]");
          if (maxBtn) {
            maxBtn.addEventListener("click", function () {
              if (document.fullscreenElement) { document.exitFullscreen(); return; }
              if (frame.requestFullscreen) {
                frame.requestFullscreen().then(fit).catch(function () {
                  window.open("/examples/agentbridge-1102-diagram.svg", "_blank", "noopener");
                });
              } else {
                window.open("/examples/agentbridge-1102-diagram.svg", "_blank", "noopener");
              }
            });
            document.addEventListener("fullscreenchange", function () { window.setTimeout(fit, 60); });
          }
          // The image is lazy, so its box may be zero until it loads; fit again when it is there.
          fit();
          if (!img.complete) img.addEventListener("load", fit, { once: true });
          window.addEventListener("resize", fit);
        })();
        </script>

        <!-- The two links the intro used to stack. One is about the engine that drew the picture
